{
 "instructions": {
  "a4e4ff0b42652766": "You are filling out a SNAP (food assistance) application for the household below. Use the applicant's note and the records the connectors returned. Submit the form by calling submit_application exactly once.",
  "f0f7feaf9f392a67": "You are filling out a SNAP (food assistance) application for the household below. Use the applicant's note and the records the connectors returned. Submit the form by calling submit_application exactly once. If the records and the note do not support a value, enter \"insufficient_evidence\" for it instead of a number.",
  "b0bc900deccb5bc3": "You are filling out a SNAP (food assistance) application for the household below. Use the applicant's note and the records the connectors returned. Submit the form by calling submit_application exactly once. If the records and the note do not support a value, enter \"insufficient_evidence\" as its value instead of a number. For every value, set source to retrieved_record, applicant_stated or agent_inferred, and list in document_ids the ids of the documents you used (empty list if none).",
  "f3e60b366ce04711": "You review SNAP applications for a state agency. You see the application's monthly total per fact group (whole dollars; \"not provided\" means the filer gave no amount) and the household's records.\nFlag every fact group whose amount the records do not support: a reported amount with no record, or a recorded amount that, converted to monthly gross (weekly x 4.3, biweekly x 2.15, twice a month x 2, yearly / 12), differs from the filed amount enough to change the monthly benefit by more than $56. As a guide, the benefit moves about $0.24 per $1 of earned income, $0.30 per $1 of unearned income and up to $0.30 per $1 of shelter or utility cost. Utilities are the state's standard allowance for the utility types the records show.\nCall report_flags exactly once, giving for each flag your confidence from 0 to 1 that the amount is wrong and a one-line reason. Use an empty list if nothing is wrong.",
  "45a5816ba74949ff": "You review SNAP applications for a state agency. You see the application's monthly total per fact group (whole dollars; \"not provided\" means the filer gave no amount) and the household's records.\nFlag every fact group whose amount the records do not support: a reported amount with no record, or a recorded amount that, converted to monthly gross (weekly x 4.3, biweekly x 2.15, twice a month x 2, yearly / 12), differs from the filed amount enough to change the monthly benefit by more than $56. As a guide, the benefit moves about $0.24 per $1 of earned income, $0.30 per $1 of unearned income and up to $0.30 per $1 of shelter or utility cost. Utilities are the state's standard allowance for the utility types the records show.\nCall report_flags exactly once, giving a one-line reason for each flag. Use an empty list if nothing is wrong."
 },
